# Ownership for static analysis, in GitHub Linguist's attributes. Code inside a git submodule
# (src/micropython, src/libs/*) is external by construction and needs no line here. A path marked
# linguist-vendored is third-party code copied into this repository; there is none today. A path
# marked linguist-generated is build output, whose findings are fixed in the generator or its
# input, so they are reported and never gate. Everything else tracked here is first-party and
# gates. A compiled path that is none of these, such as an untracked file outside the build
# directories, fails the analysis rather than defaulting to a class.
#
# The build directories are ignored by git, so these lines only ever classify, never change how a
# tracked file is diffed. The unix port's own build output sits inside src/micropython and is
# external for that reason.
src/system/build-*/** linguist-generated
src/unix/build/** linguist-generated
